[{"id":272,"name":"Learning.IdentAlg.IsRun.klDiv_map_out_le_tsum_compProd","kind":"Lemma","keyword":"lemma","module":"Maiti2026Power.LeanMachineLearning.RunDivergence","package":"Maiti2026Power","isProp":true,"hashes":{"meaning":"a2db6bb3a9f3efa3","local":"9456b576c3b231a2","content":"afbbfe3f7fc70cc7"},"doc":"**Change of measure at a stopping time**, composition-product form: for two runs of the same\nidentification algorithm in two stationary environments with reward kernels `κ` and `κ'`, with\nalmost surely finite stopping times, the divergence between the laws of the outputs is at most\nthe series over the rounds `t` of the conditional divergences of the reward kernels given the\nplayed action, on the event that the algorithm has not stopped after `t` rounds. ","statement":{"binders":[{"explicit":false,"name":"𝓐","role":"type","type":"Type u_1"},{"explicit":false,"name":"𝓨","role":"type","type":"Type u_2"},{"explicit":false,"name":"𝓓","role":"type","type":"Type u_3"},{"explicit":false,"name":"m𝓐","role":"instance","type":"MeasurableSpace 𝓐"},{"explicit":false,"name":"m𝓨","role":"instance","type":"MeasurableSpace 𝓨"},{"explicit":false,"name":"m𝓓","role":"instance","type":"MeasurableSpace 𝓓"},{"explicit":false,"name":"Ω","role":"type","type":"Type u_4"},{"explicit":false,"name":"Ω'","role":"type","type":"Type u_5"},{"explicit":false,"name":"mΩ","role":"instance","type":"MeasurableSpace Ω"},{"explicit":false,"name":"mΩ'","role":"instance","type":"MeasurableSpace Ω'"},{"explicit":false,"name":"P","role":"variable","type":"MeasureTheory.Measure Ω"},{"explicit":false,"name":"P'","role":"variable","type":"MeasureTheory.Measure Ω'"},{"explicit":false,"name":"","role":"instance","type":"MeasureTheory.IsProbabilityMeasure P"},{"explicit":false,"name":"","role":"instance","type":"MeasureTheory.IsProbabilityMeasure P'"},{"explicit":false,"name":"A","role":"variable","type":"IdentAlg Unit 𝓐 𝓨 𝓓"},{"explicit":false,"name":"O","role":"variable","type":"ℕ → Ω → Unit"},{"explicit":false,"name":"X","role":"variable","type":"ℕ → Ω → 𝓐"},{"explicit":false,"name":"Y","role":"variable","type":"ℕ → Ω → 𝓨"},{"explicit":false,"name":"O'","role":"variable","type":"ℕ → Ω' → Unit"},{"explicit":false,"name":"X'","role":"variable","type":"ℕ → Ω' → 𝓐"},{"explicit":false,"name":"Y'","role":"variable","type":"ℕ → Ω' → 𝓨"},{"explicit":false,"name":"out","role":"variable","type":"Ω → 𝓓"},{"explicit":false,"name":"out'","role":"variable","type":"Ω' → 𝓓"},{"explicit":false,"name":"κ","role":"variable","type":"ProbabilityTheory.Kernel 𝓐 𝓨"},{"explicit":false,"name":"κ'","role":"variable","type":"ProbabilityTheory.Kernel 𝓐 𝓨"},{"explicit":false,"name":"","role":"instance","type":"ProbabilityTheory.IsMarkovKernel κ"},{"explicit":false,"name":"","role":"instance","type":"ProbabilityTheory.IsMarkovKernel κ'"},{"explicit":true,"name":"h","role":"hypothesis","type":"A.IsRun (stationaryEnv κ) O X Y out P"},{"explicit":true,"name":"h'","role":"hypothesis","type":"A.IsRun (stationaryEnv κ') O' X' Y' out' P'"},{"explicit":true,"name":"hτ","role":"hypothesis","type":"∀ᵐ (ω : Ω) ∂P, A.stoppingTime O X Y ω ≠ ⊤"},{"explicit":true,"name":"hτ'","role":"hypothesis","type":"∀ᵐ (ω : Ω') ∂P', A.stoppingTime O' X' Y' ω ≠ ⊤"}],"conclusion":"InformationTheory.klDiv (MeasureTheory.Measure.map out P) (MeasureTheory.Measure.map out' P') ≤\n  ∑' (t : ℕ),\n    InformationTheory.klDiv\n      ((MeasureTheory.Measure.map (X t) (P.restrict {ω | ↑t < A.stoppingTime O X Y ω})).compProd κ)\n      ((MeasureTheory.Measure.map (X t) (P.restrict {ω | ↑t < A.stoppingTime O X Y ω})).compProd κ')","decl":"Learning.IdentAlg.IsRun.klDiv_map_out_le_tsum_compProd"},"code":"/-- **Change of measure at a stopping time**, composition-product form: for two runs of the same\nidentification algorithm in two stationary environments with reward kernels `κ` and `κ'`, with\nalmost surely finite stopping times, the divergence between the laws of the outputs is at most\nthe series over the rounds `t` of the conditional divergences of the reward kernels given the\nplayed action, on the event that the algorithm has not stopped after `t` rounds. -/\nlemma IsRun.klDiv_map_out_le_tsum_compProd (h : A.IsRun (stationaryEnv κ) O X Y out P)\n    (h' : A.IsRun (stationaryEnv κ') O' X' Y' out' P') (hτ : ∀ᵐ ω ∂P, A.stoppingTime O X Y ω ≠ ⊤)\n    (hτ' : ∀ᵐ ω ∂P', A.stoppingTime O' X' Y' ω ≠ ⊤) :\n    klDiv (P.map out) (P'.map out') ≤\n      ∑' t : ℕ, klDiv ((P.restrict {ω | (t : ℕ∞) < A.stoppingTime O X Y ω}).map (X t) ⊗ₘ κ)\n        ((P.restrict {ω | (t : ℕ∞) < A.stoppingTime O X Y ω}).map (X t) ⊗ₘ κ')","proof":":=\n  (h.klDiv_map_out_le_stoppedHist h').trans_eq\n    (h.isAlgEnvSeq.klDiv_map_stoppedValue_sigmaHistory_compProd h'.isAlgEnvSeq\n      A.measurableSet_stopSet hτ hτ')","source":{"path":"Maiti2026Power/LeanMachineLearning/RunDivergence.lean","start":71,"end":84,"url":"https://github.com/RemyDegenne/colt-2026-83/blob/3f6c0f296a3b7e4aa8fe333225505f5b2f61f9e0/Maiti2026Power/LeanMachineLearning/RunDivergence.lean#L71-L84"},"deps":[],"outside":[],"external":[["ENNReal","mathlib","definition"],["ENNReal.instAddCommMonoid","mathlib","instance"],["ENNReal.instLE","mathlib","instance"],["ENNReal.instTopologicalSpace","mathlib","instance"],["ENat","mathlib","definition"],["ENat.instNatCast","mathlib","instance"],["Filter.Eventually","mathlib","definition"],["InformationTheory.klDiv","mathlib","definition"],["LE.le","lean4","definition"],["LT.lt","lean4","definition"],["Learning.IdentAlg","LeanMachineLearning","structure"],["Learning.IdentAlg.IsRun","LeanMachineLearning","structure"],["Learning.IdentAlg.stoppingTime","LeanMachineLearning","definition"],["Learning.stationaryEnv","LeanMachineLearning","definition"],["MeasurableSpace","mathlib","class"],["MeasureTheory.IsProbabilityMeasure","mathlib","class"],["MeasureTheory.IsZeroOrProbabilityMeasure.toIsFiniteMeasure","mathlib","instance"],["MeasureTheory.Measure","mathlib","structure"],["MeasureTheory.Measure.compProd","mathlib","definition"